{"name":"Canteen","hex":"#5e5347","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"canteen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A water bottle, flask, or other vessel, typically used by a soldier or camper as a bottle for carrying water or liquor for drink.","A military mess kit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/canteen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Canteen (bottle)","blocks":[{"text":"A canteen is a reusable drinking water bottle designed to be used by hikers, campers, soldiers, bush firefighters, and workers in the field. It is usually fitted with a shoulder strap or means for fastening it to a belt, and may be covered with a cloth bag and padding to protect the bottle and insulate the contents. If the padding is soaked with water, evaporative cooling can help keep the contents of the bottle cool. Many canteens also include a nested canteen cup."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Military_Canteen_7984.jpg/330px-Military_Canteen_7984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canteen_(bottle)"},{"title":"Cafeteria","blocks":[{"text":"A cafeteria, sometimes called a canteen outside North America, is a type of food service location in which there is no waiting staff table service. Cafeterias are different from coffeehouses, although the English term came from the Spanish term cafetería, which carries the same meaning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Infosys.Electronic.City.Cafeteria.JPG/330px-Infosys.Electronic.City.Cafeteria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cafeteria"},{"title":"Canteen (charity)","blocks":[{"text":"Canteen is an Australian not-for-profit cancer charity that provides free and tailored support to young people aged 12–25 who are impacted by cancer. Whether they are dealing with their own diagnosis, a close family member's cancer or the death of a loved one, Canteen provides a wide range of free support services to help them overcome the specific challenges they're dealing with. Canteen also provides services for parents dealing with cancer in their family. The CEO of Canteen is Siona Hardy."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canteen_(charity)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Alamannic_Canteen.JPG/500px-Alamannic_Canteen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Alamannic_Canteen.JPG/1280px-Alamannic_Canteen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Alamannic_Canteen.JPG/500px-Alamannic_Canteen.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wooden canteen from Oberflacht, Germany (7th century)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlamannic_Canteen.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Cafeteria_Server.jpg/500px-Cafeteria_Server.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Cafeteria_Server.jpg/500px-Cafeteria_Server.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hospital cafeteria tray line server in Port Charlotte, Florida","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACafeteria_Server.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Postcard_from_Childs_Philadelphia_1908.jpg/500px-Postcard_from_Childs_Philadelphia_1908.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Postcard_from_Childs_Philadelphia_1908.jpg/1280px-Postcard_from_Childs_Philadelphia_1908.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte